    "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are a helpful assistant.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nThe arithmetic mean (or average) of $A$, $B$ and $C$ is 10. The value of $A$ is six less than the value of $B$, and the value of $C$ is three more than the value of $B$. What is the value of $C$?\n\nThink step by step inside <think> </think> tags, then give your final answer inside \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\nTo solve for the value of \\( C \\), we start by using the information given in the problem. The arithmetic mean of \\( A \\), \\( B \\), and \\( C \\) is 10. This can be expressed as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{A + B + C}{3} = 10\n\\]\n\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we get:\n\n\\[\nA + B + C = 30\n\\]\n\nWe are also given that \\( A \\) is six less than \\( B \\), which can be written as:\n\n\\[\nA = B - 6\n\\]\n\nAdditionally, \\( C \\) is three more than \\( B \\), which can be written as:\n\n\\[\nC = B + 3\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( A \\) and \\( C \\) in terms of \\( B \\) into the equation \\( A + B + C = 30 \\):\n\n\\[\n(B - 6) + B + (B + 3) = 30\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\nB - 6 + B + B + 3 = 30\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n3B - 3 = 30\n\\]\n\nAdd 3 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n3B = 33\n\\]\n\nDivide by 3:\n\n\\[\nB = 11\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\( B = 11 \\), we can find \\( A \\) and \\( C \\):\n\n\\[\nA = B - 6 = 11 - 6 = 5\n\\]\n\n\\[\nC = B + 3 = 11 + 3 = 14\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( C \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{14}\n\\]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nReview the solution above. Identify and correct any errors; if it is correct, retain its answer. Give your final answer inside \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n",
